IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er5-pilot-24`

-- Tests of er5-pilot-24 (regs 77.995 to 77.999). Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the Regulations
-- (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1614-1638), before the run, beside the assertion. The figures in the 77.999(4)(a) test (a base of 45 weeks)
-- are invented for the test: the base comes from s 12(2) of the Act (piece ei1) and no published figure is used.

§ `Reg 77.995 - the purpose`

-- src:1614: the purpose is "testing the outcomes of applying certain employment insurance measures to respond to the impacts on employment of major changes in economic conditions".
#ASSERT `reg 77.995 the purpose of Pilot Project No. 24` EQUALS "testing the outcomes of applying certain employment insurance measures to respond to the impacts on employment of major changes in economic conditions"

§ `Reg 77.996 - the waiting period may be waived (src:1617)`

-- A benefit period that begins on March 30, 2025, the first day of the period: within it, so the waiver is possible.
#ASSERT `reg 77.996 the Commission may waive the waiting period` (YMD 2025 3 30)
-- The day before the period: outside it.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.996 the Commission may waive the waiting period` (YMD 2025 3 29))
-- October 10, 2026, the last day of the period: within it.
#ASSERT `reg 77.996 the Commission may waive the waiting period` (YMD 2026 10 10)
-- The day after the period: outside it.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.996 the Commission may waive the waiting period` (YMD 2026 10 11))
-- A benefit period in the middle of the period.
#ASSERT `reg 77.996 the Commission may waive the waiting period` (YMD 2025 12 25)

-- The waiver needs both the power (the benefit period begins in the period) and the Commission's decision to waive.
#ASSERT `reg 77.996 the waiting period is waived` (YMD 2025 6 1) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.996 the waiting period is waived` (YMD 2025 6 1) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.996 the waiting period is waived` (YMD 2027 1 1) TRUE)

§ `Reg 77.997 - lay-off or separation earnings (src:1620-1622)`

-- Earnings that are not paid by reason of a lay-off or separation are outside this section, whatever the dates.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.997 earnings paid by reason of a lay-off or separation do not constitute earnings for the purposes of subsection 35(2)` FALSE (YMD 2025 6 1) (YMD 2025 6 1))
-- (a): the benefit period begins on March 30, 2025, the first day of the period.
#ASSERT `reg 77.997 earnings paid by reason of a lay-off or separation do not constitute earnings for the purposes of subsection 35(2)` TRUE (YMD 2025 3 30) (YMD 2025 3 30)
-- (a): the benefit period begins on October 10, 2026, the last day.
#ASSERT `reg 77.997 earnings paid by reason of a lay-off or separation do not constitute earnings for the purposes of subsection 35(2)` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 10) (YMD 2026 10 4)
-- Neither (a) nor (b): the benefit period began on March 29, 2025 and the first week of allocation is the week of Sunday March 23, 2025.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.997 earnings paid by reason of a lay-off or separation do not constitute earnings for the purposes of subsection 35(2)` TRUE (YMD 2025 3 29) (YMD 2025 3 23))
-- (b): the benefit period began before the period, and the first week of allocation is the week of Sunday March 30, 2025, which falls within it.
#ASSERT `reg 77.997 earnings paid by reason of a lay-off or separation do not constitute earnings for the purposes of subsection 35(2)` TRUE (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 3 30)
-- (b): the first week of allocation is the week of Sunday October 4, 2026, which ends on Saturday October 10, 2026: it falls within the period.
#ASSERT `reg 77.997 earnings paid by reason of a lay-off or separation do not constitute earnings for the purposes of subsection 35(2)` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2026 10 4)
-- (b): the first week of allocation is the week of Sunday October 11, 2026: it falls after the period.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.997 earnings paid by reason of a lay-off or separation do not constitute earnings for the purposes of subsection 35(2)` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2026 10 11))

§ `Reg 77.998 - the regional rate of unemployment (src:1625-1628)`

-- Rates are fractions: 6.1% is 0.061. The later week begins on Sunday April 6, 2025, the first day of the window.
-- (a): a section 17 rate of 6.1% or less is deemed to be 7.1%.
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 4 6) 0.061 EQUALS 0.071
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 4 6) 0.05 EQUALS 0.071
-- (b): more than 6.1% and less than 12.1%: the rate plus 1%. Just above the boundary at 6.1%:
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 4 6) 0.0611 EQUALS 0.0711
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 4 6) 0.09 EQUALS 0.10
-- (b): just below the boundary at 12.1%.
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 4 6) 0.1209 EQUALS 0.1309
-- (c): 12.1% or greater, but less than 13.1%: deemed to be 13.1%.
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 4 6) 0.121 EQUALS 0.131
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 4 6) 0.13 EQUALS 0.131
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 4 6) 0.1309 EQUALS 0.131
-- A rate that is not less than 13.1% is outside the section: nothing is deemed, the section 17 rate stays.
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 4 6) 0.131 EQUALS 0.131
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 4 6) 0.14 EQUALS 0.14
-- The window: a later week beginning March 30, 2025 is before April 6, 2025, so the rate stays.
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 3 30) 0.05 EQUALS 0.05
-- A later week beginning on October 5, 2025 is inside the window; on the last day, October 11, 2025, also inside.
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 10 5) 0.05 EQUALS 0.071
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 10 11) 0.05 EQUALS 0.071
-- Beginning on October 12, 2025 is after the window: the rate stays.
#ASSERT `reg 77.998 the regional rate of unemployment that applies to the claimant` (YMD 2025 10 12) 0.05 EQUALS 0.05

§ `Reg 77.999(1) - long-tenured worker (src:1631)`

-- Less than 36 weeks of regular benefits (35), and 7 of the 10 years, with the return for the year before assessed: a long-tenured worker.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(1) long-tenured worker` 35 TRUE 7 0
-- 36 weeks is not less than 36.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.999(1) long-tenured worker` 36 TRUE 10 0)
-- Only 6 of the 10 years.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.999(1) long-tenured worker` 0 TRUE 6 10)
-- The return for the year before has not been assessed: the 10 years before that year count, so 7 there is enough though the other count is 3.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(1) long-tenured worker` 0 FALSE 3 7
-- The return is not assessed and the earlier ten years give only 6, whatever the other count says.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.999(1) long-tenured worker` 0 FALSE 10 6)

§ `Reg 77.999(2) - the benefit period is extended by 20 weeks (src:1632)`

-- Every condition met: established under s 9, begins June 15, 2025 (the first day), never ended early, long-tenured, at least one week paid. Commencement taken as July 1, 2025.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(2) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE (YMD 2025 6 15) NOTHING (YMD 2025 7 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS 20
-- Begins on October 10, 2026, the last day of the period.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(2) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 10) NOTHING (YMD 2025 7 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS 20
-- Begins on June 14, 2025, the day before the period: nothing.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(2) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE (YMD 2025 6 14) NOTHING (YMD 2025 7 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS 0
-- Begins on October 11, 2026, the day after the period: nothing.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(2) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 11) NOTHING (YMD 2025 7 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS 0
-- Ended under paragraph 10(8)(d) on June 20, 2025, before the section came into force on July 1, 2025: not extended.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(2) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE (YMD 2025 6 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 6 20)) (YMD 2025 7 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS 0
-- Ended on July 1, 2025, the day it came into force, which is not before that day: still extended.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(2) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE (YMD 2025 6 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 7 1)) (YMD 2025 7 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS 20
-- Ended later than the day it came into force: still extended.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(2) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE (YMD 2025 6 15) (JUST (YMD 2025 9 1)) (YMD 2025 7 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS 20
-- Not a long-tenured worker.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(2) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE (YMD 2025 6 15) NOTHING (YMD 2025 7 1) FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0
-- No week of regular or section 25 benefits paid.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(2) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` TRUE (YMD 2025 6 15) NOTHING (YMD 2025 7 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- Not established under section 9.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(2) the number of weeks by which the benefit period is extended` FALSE (YMD 2025 6 15) NOTHING (YMD 2025 7 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS 0

§ `Reg 77.999(3) - held to 104 weeks (src:1633-1634)`

-- A benefit period beginning in the period whose extensions would make it 110 weeks: held to 104.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(3) the length in weeks of the benefit period after its extensions, held to 104 weeks` (YMD 2025 7 6) 110 EQUALS JUST 104
-- Exactly 104 is not more than 104.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(3) the length in weeks of the benefit period after its extensions, held to 104 weeks` (YMD 2025 7 6) 104 EQUALS JUST 104
-- 90 weeks is below the limit.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(3) the length in weeks of the benefit period after its extensions, held to 104 weeks` (YMD 2025 7 6) 90 EQUALS JUST 90
-- Outside the period the section adapts nothing: the Act's own subsection 10(14) governs, outside this piece.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(3) the length in weeks of the benefit period after its extensions, held to 104 weeks` (YMD 2027 1 3) 110 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 77.999(4) - the maximum weeks and the 50-week reference (src:1635-1637)`

-- Extended: a base of 45 weeks (invented for the test) becomes 65.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(4)(a) the maximum number of weeks of benefits for a reason other than one mentioned in subsection 12(3) of the Act` 45 TRUE EQUALS 65
-- Not extended: unchanged.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(4)(a) the maximum number of weeks of benefits for a reason other than one mentioned in subsection 12(3) of the Act` 45 FALSE EQUALS 45
-- Extended: the reference to 50 weeks in subsection 12(6) is read as 70.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(4)(b) the number of weeks that subsection 12(6) of the Act refers to` TRUE EQUALS 70
-- Not extended: the Act's 50.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(4)(b) the number of weeks that subsection 12(6) of the Act refers to` FALSE EQUALS 50

§ `Reg 77.999(5) - ceasing to be long-tenured does not end the extra weeks (src:1638)`

-- Extended, the claimant ceases to be a long-tenured worker, no other reason: the weeks are still payable.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(5) the additional weeks are still payable` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- The same without the cessation: the cessation made no difference.
#ASSERT `reg 77.999(5) the additional weeks are still payable` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Some other reason ends the right: not payable.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.999(5) the additional weeks are still payable` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- Not extended: there are no additional weeks.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.999(5) the additional weeks are still payable` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
